OSNS_generic
------------

OSNS generic program, which does start other modules/services. The funtionality lies in these modules,
OSNS_genric self offers nothing.

By default it reads the profile like:

OSNS_generic --profile=mount

or

OSNS_generic --profile=dnssd

These profiles are files, which are located at:

/etc/osns/start

These files contain information about what modules to load, and how. For example, the "dnssd" profile looks like:

osns_net_dnssd.so action

means OSNS_generic will load the osns_net_dnssd.so module, and will look for the struct osns_ctx_action_s, and will
start the member "manage" to start functionality this module has. For example:

to start the dnssd service (send dns sd requests, process the replies, maintain a local db as cache of local hosts and services),
the osns_ctx_action_s struct has to be used, to browse the services found in the db, this is not required.





